WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.510
In 961 Ani became the capital
of Bagratid Armenia,

2
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.256
a city on a plateau
above the Akhurian gorge.

3
00:00:11.296 --> 00:00:13.866
King Hovhannes-Smbat had no son,

4
00:00:13.906 --> 00:00:18.395
and he willed that after his death,
Ani would pass to the empire.

5
00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:20.465
He died around 1041,

6
00:00:20.505 --> 00:00:23.917
and imperial troops
came to take the city.

7
00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:28.707
Armenian chroniclers tell how
the sparapet Vahram Pahlavuni

8
00:00:28.747 --> 00:00:34.135
led the Armenians out and routed
an imperial army under the walls.

9
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:38.817
He raised the late king's
young nephew, Gagik II, to the throne.

10
00:00:39.177 --> 00:00:43.328
The emperor's armies came again,
and failed to take the city.

11
00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:46.969
No Byzantine army
ever took Ani by storm.

12
00:00:47.009 --> 00:00:51.839
But in 1045, while Gagik
was held in Constantinople,

13
00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:54.564
Ani was handed over to the empire.

14
00:00:54.924 --> 00:00:59.145
Stand with Vahram,
and keep the young king's crown.

